    "https://careers.viu.ca/vacancy/opportunity-profile-president-and-vicechancellor-603792.html": {
      "title": "OPPORTUNITY PROFILE: President and Vice-Chancellor  (2990)",
      "description": "OPPORTUNITY PROFILE: President and Vice-Chancellor  (2990) | VIU | Vancouver Island University Skip to main content VIU Future Students International Students Current Students Employees Alumni & Donors Contact Registration Registration Space tasks Map Members Space Structure Registration Site map Parents viu.ca Sections Pages All Sites... All Groups... Site Members Registration Member list Admins admin boquist culvers manhasm2 testuser Members No members OPPORTUNITY PROFILE: President and Vice-Chancellor  (2990) OPPORTUNITY PROFILE: President and Vice-Chancellor Vancouver Island University (VIU) is pleased to partner with an external search firm in the recruitment of its next President and Vice‑Chancellor. This is a meaningful leadership opportunity to serve a university that is deeply connected to its communities and committed to student success, access, and inclusion. We invite you to learn more about this role and the impact it will have in guiding VIU through its next chapter, one that builds on strong relationships, honours our connection to place, and supports continued growth and transformation, by reviewing the attached opportunity profile. Please note that all inquiries and applications are being managed directly through the search firm, as outlined in the profile. VIU offers a competitive compensation package which includes an attractive base salary and excellent benefits, including a defined benefits pension plan. The compensation range for this role is $245,000 - $288,000. Further details will be discussed with candidates during the interview process. Employment Group ADMIN Position Number 00256 Division President Department Office of the President Campus Nanaimo campus  *Successful candidates must be able to attend in person on campus as required. Location Nanaimo, British Columbia Country Canada Appointment Type regular full-time Additional Information Open until filled. Applications will be managed through the Search firm. Please see contact information below. Posted Date 26-Jun-2026 Job Reference 2990 Documents President Profile (Word , 55.46kb) This search is being supported by Boyden. To submit your CV and letter of introduction for consideration, in confidence, please go to: https://boyden.thriveapp.ly/job/3323 For more information, please contact: Kathryn Young, Managing Partner kyoung@boyden.com | 604-376-4898 Apply for this job Print this job Send to a friend About VIU Careers at VIU Employee Directory Parking Academics International Students Library Programs and Courses VIU Learn Campuses Nanaimo (Main Campus) Cowichan Parksville-Qualicum Centre tiwšɛmawtxʷ (Powell River) About VIU Why VIU? Careers at VIU Employee Directory VIU Facts Events News Parking University Governance Academics Admission Requirements Dual Credit Financial Aid and Awards Graduate Programs International Students Library Online Education Programs and Courses Registration Transfer Students VIU Learn Student Life Student Housing Campus Recreation Campus Store Food Services Health and Wellness Services for Students VIU Mariners Athletics Campuses Campus Information Nanaimo (Main Campus) Cowichan Parksville-Qualicum Centre tiwšɛmawtxʷ (Powell River) Vancouver Island University Nanaimo (Main Campus) 900 Fifth Street Nanaimo, BC V9R 5S5 Canada 250.753.3245 1.888.920.2221 info@viu.ca Facebook Instagram Twitter Youtube LinkedIn VIU RSS feed The VIU community acknowledges and thanks the Snuneymuxw, Quw’utsun and Tla’amin, on whose traditional lands we teach, learn,\n                                                                                        research, live and share knowledge. Accreditation Terms Emergency Information Website Feedback © 2021 Vancouver Island University MENU CLOSE X Future Students International Students Current Students Employees Alumni & Donors Contact VIU Main Menu Open submenu (About VIU) About VIU Open submenu (Programs and Courses) Programs and Courses Open submenu (Admissions) Admissions