    "https://careers.viu.ca/vacancy/instructors-practical-nursing-603686.html": {
      "title": "Instructors, Practical Nursing  (2955)",
      "description": "Instructors, Practical Nursing  (2955) | VIU | Vancouver Island University Skip to main content VIU Future Students International Students Current Students Employees Alumni & Donors Contact Registration Registration Space tasks Map Members Space Structure Registration Site map Parents viu.ca Sections Pages All Sites... All Groups... Site Members Registration Member list Admins admin boquist culvers manhasm2 testuser Members No members Instructors, Practical Nursing  (2955) Instructors, Practical Nursing The Faculty of Health Sciences and Human Services includes the Departments of Child and Youth Care, Dental Assistant, Dental Hygiene, Health Care Assistant, Nursing, Practical Nursing, Social Work, Kinesiology, and a Professional Development and Training department. The mission of the Faculty is to foster student success and develop and maintain relevant, responsive, and stimulating learning opportunities that are community-based, globally and locally, and offered in a visionary, interprofessional environment that is conducive to learning and promotes health and wellness for all. The Dean and the Dean's Office lead, manage, administer and support the instructional, scholarly and outreach activities of the Faculty on four campuses with this mission in mind. VIU is seeking dynamic nursing instructors to deliver a variety of courses (some virtual) within the Practical Nursing (PN) program at our Nanaimo, and tiwšɛmawtxʷ campuses for the 2026/2027 academic year. For a complete listing of our course offerings please visit https://www.viu.ca/programs/health/practical-nursing Employment Group BCGEU Position Number 00206 Division Faculty of Health Sciences and Human Services Department Practical Nursing Campus Multiple locations  *Successful candidates must able to attend in person on campus as required. Location Nanaimo, British Columbia Country Canada Appointment Type temporary part-time Workload Up to 28 hours per week of direct instruction Pay Level BCGEU: $71,846 - $115,129 per annum (prorated if part-time). Starting Salary Faculty are placed on the BCGEU salary scale based on education, experience and placement criteria as outlined in the Collective Agreement, to an initial maximum of $89,412 per annum Start: Start and end dates would correlate with the specific term up to June 30, 2027 Appointment Start Date 25-Jun-2026 Appointment End Date 30-Jun-2027 Applicant Documents CV/Resume,\nCover Letter,\nQualifications ,\nName and contact information of recent supervisors willing to provide a reference Posted Date 21-May-2026 Closing Date 19-May-2027 Job Reference 2955 Duties: PN Instructors participate in wide variety of teaching and learning opportunities in clinical, lab and classroom settings including: the preparation and delivery of class content; the design and grading of student assignments and tests; and, the facilitation of student integration of theory and practice. The successful candidate will have the ability to work in a team-oriented Faculty in an institution that is primarily focused on students and teaching. Candidates must be able to foster student success, develop stimulating learning opportunities and participate in instructional advising with students. Candidates will also participate in activities outside the classroom including departmental and faculty meetings, contribute to program activities related to curriculum and administrative planning activities. Required Qualifications: Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSN) from an appropriately accredited institution with current practicing BC College of Nurses and Midwives (BCCNM) in good standing; Licensed Practical Nurse (LPN) from an appropriately accredited institution with current practicing BC College of Nurses and Midwifes (BCCNM) in good standing; The BC Provincial Instructor Diploma Program, or its equivalent, completed or in progress, or a commitment to engage in the training (maximum two years to completion) from an accredited institution A minimum of five years recent medical, surgical and gerontological nursing experience; Familiar with practice settings in Central Vancouver Island including community, gerontology and acute care; Responsive to a diverse student population; A solid understanding of the scope and role of LPNs in the Health Care System; Proficiency with the application and integration of information technology; Knowledge and understanding of Aboriginal ways of knowing and cultural teachings. Must possess a valid Class 5 BC Driver's License and have a confirmed satisfactory driving record. Some positions require travel to a variety of practice locations. Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree in nursing or related field from an appropriately accredited institution. Experience teaching adults in a post-secondary setting. Familiarity with computer applications and learning management systems (D2L) in an educational setting. Apply for this job Print this job Send to a friend About VIU Careers at VIU Employee Directory Parking Academics International Students Library Programs and Courses VIU Learn Campuses Nanaimo (Main Campus) Cowichan Parksville-Qualicum Centre tiwšɛmawtxʷ (Powell River) About VIU Why VIU? Careers at VIU Employee Directory VIU Facts Events News Parking University Governance Academics Admission Requirements Dual Credit Financial Aid and Awards Graduate Programs International Students Library Online Education Programs and Courses Registration Transfer Students VIU Learn Student Life Student Housing Campus Recreation Campus Store Food Services Health and Wellness Services for Students VIU Mariners Athletics Campuses Campus Information Nanaimo (Main Campus) Cowichan Parksville-Qualicum Centre tiwšɛmawtxʷ (Powell River) Vancouver Island University Nanaimo (Main Campus) 900 Fifth Street Nanaimo, BC V9R 5S5 Canada 250.753.3245 1.888.920.2221 info@viu.ca Facebook Instagram Twitter Youtube LinkedIn VIU RSS feed The VIU community acknowledges and thanks the Snuneymuxw, Quw’utsun and Tla’amin, on whose traditional lands we teach, learn,\n                                                                                        research, live and share knowledge. Accreditation Terms Emergency Information Website Feedback © 2021 Vancouver Island University MENU CLOSE X Future Students International Students Current Students Employees Alumni & Donors Contact VIU Main Menu Open submenu (About VIU) About VIU Open submenu (Programs and Courses) Programs and Courses Open submenu (Admissions) Admissions Facebook Instagram Twitter Youtube LinkedIn VIU RSS feed Close submenu (About VIU) About VIU Why VIU Campus Information Athletics Close submenu (Programs and Courses) Programs and Courses Open submenu (Areas of Study) Areas of Study Courses Apply Now Close submenu (Areas of Study) Areas of Study Open submenu (Academic and Career Preparation) Academic and Career Preparation Open submenu (Art, Design and Performing Arts) Art, Design and Performing Arts Open submenu (Arts, Humanities and Social Sciences) Arts, Humanities and Social Sciences Open submenu (Business Management) Business Management Open submenu (Education) Education English as a Second Language (ESL) Exploratory University Studies Open submenu (First Nations) First Nations Graduate Programs Open submenu (Health) Health Open submenu (Human Services) Human Services Natural Resource Extension Program Online Programs / Distance Courses Open submenu (Professional Development and Training) Professional Development and Training Open submenu (Science and Technology) Science and Technology The High School at VIU Open submenu (Tourism, Recreation and Hospitality) Tourism, Recreation and Hospitality Open submenu (Trades and Applied Technology) Trades and Applied Technology Teaching English as a Second or Foreign Language Close submenu (Academic and Career Preparation) Academic and Career Preparation Aboriginal University Bridging Program Certificate Employability Skills Program Foundations for Suc