    "https://careers.viu.ca/vacancy/cooks-extended-381318.html": {
      "title": "Cook(s) (Extended) (2926)",
      "description": "Cook(s) (Extended) (2926) | VIU | Vancouver Island University Skip to main content VIU Future Students International Students Current Students Employees Alumni & Donors Contact Registration Registration Space tasks Map Members Space Structure Registration Site map Parents viu.ca Sections Pages All Sites... All Groups... Site Members Registration Member list Admins admin boquist culvers manhasm2 testuser Members No members Cook(s) (Extended) (2926) Cook(s) (Extended) Employment Group CUPE Position Number 00495 Division VP Administration and Finance Department Cafeteria Campus Nanaimo campus  *Successful candidates must be able to attend in person on campus as required. Location Nanaimo, British Columbia Country Canada Appointment Type temporary part-time Workload 0-35 hours per week depending upon operational need. Shift-based work 7 days per week morning, afternoon, and evening shifts. Pay Level CUPE 5: $27.78 per hour Start: As soon as possible. Appointment End Date 31-Mar-2027 Additional Information Appointment may end early or be extended. Multiple positions available. Applications will be reviewed on a continuous basis. Applicant Documents CV/Resume,\nName and contact information of recent supervisors willing to provide a reference Posted Date 23-Apr-2026 Closing Date 31-Mar-2027 Job Reference 2926 Documents CUPE Self-Declaration Form (Word , 40.35kb) Duties: We are looking for energetic and creative Cooks to prepare delicious dishes in our Cafeteria. Cooks prepare meals, monitors food levels, ensures all food is of high quality and provides service to the Campus Community. The ideal candidate would have excellent communication skills and ability to work in a fast paced environment. Must be willing to take direction and follow guidelines provided as well as adhere to all health and safety requirements. Under the direction of the kitchen supervisor or shift lead, the Cook will prepare food as per the daily task list and Food Safety Guidelines as outlined in the duties below. Cook all food in various cooking methods including appetizers, entrees and desserts Ensure meals are prepared and served with in the designated meal period while interacting with Customers Train new cooks and prep cooks on specific tasks as assign Provide creative menu suggestions to Kitchen Supervisor Maintain a clean and orderly kitchen by washing dishes/ pots, cleaning work stations/kitchen as needed and sanitizing surfaces. Monitor station inventory levels and adhere to all food safety and sanitation guidelines Ensure that all food is of high quality and meets our standards Follow recipes and established cooking techniques to ensure consistency. Collaborate with other kitchen staff to ensure that all meals and food items are prepared and served in a timely manner Perform other kitchen duties as assigned Required Qualifications: One year Culinary Arts Certificate Program and a minimum of 3 years experience. A combination of experience and education may be considered. FoodSafe certificate Exceptional culinary skills and ability to follow recipes utilizing a variety of cooking techniques Knowledge and previous experience using all standard kitchen equipment Knowledge of all health and safety regulations for proper food handling, storage and serving Manual dexterity able to operate cutting tools and kitchen utensils Exceptional organizational and time management skills as well as attention to detail Friendly disposition when interacting with customers Ability to stay calm and stay positive under pressure A team player with good communication skills Ability to stand for extended periods of time and lift up to 30 KG Preferred Qualifications: Red Seal Certification VIU is pleased to offer eligible employees a comprehensive benefit plan; ample paid holiday time; professional development opportunities and a desirable pension plan. As part of the VIU campus community, our employees work with supportive colleagues within an encouraging environment and are provided with the tools and training that promote learning and development. The perks of VIU employment are multiple, and include well-being initiatives and services, strategic discounts, and flexible work opportunities. Note: Short-listed candidates must provide original transcripts, or applicable original certifications at time of interview. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Vancouver Island University (VIU) is collectively committed to building and sustaining a diverse and inclusive working and learning environment for faculty, staff, and students.  In our journey towards greater diversity, we invite applications from members of equity-seeking communities including women, racialized and Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, persons of all gender identities and sexual orientations who bring value to the VIU community through their lived experiences.  We encourage members of all equity-seeking groups to self-identify within their application cover letter.  When a candidate voluntarily discloses this information in their cover letter, the information will be used only for the fulfillment of the career opportunity.  Disclosure and/or self-identification with an equity-seeking group will not lead to advantageous treatment of a candidate who is not qualified. Apply for this job Print this job Send to a friend About VIU Careers at VIU Employee Directory Parking Academics International Students Library Programs and Courses VIU Learn Campuses Nanaimo (Main Campus) Cowichan Parksville-Qualicum Centre tiwšɛmawtxʷ (Powell River) About VIU Why VIU? Careers at VIU Employee Directory VIU Facts Events News Parking University Governance Academics Admission Requirements Dual Credit Financial Aid and Awards Graduate Programs International Students Library Online Education Programs and Courses Registration Transfer Students VIU Learn Student Life Student Housing Campus Recreation Campus Store Food Services Health and Wellness Services for Students VIU Mariners Athletics Campuses Campus Information Nanaimo (Main Campus) Cowichan Parksville-Qualicum Centre tiwšɛmawtxʷ (Powell River) Vancouver Island University Nanaimo (Main Campus) 900 Fifth Street Nanaimo, BC V9R 5S5 Canada 250.753.3245 1.888.920.2221 info@viu.ca Facebook Instagram Twitter Youtube LinkedIn VIU RSS feed The VIU community acknowledges and thanks the Snuneymuxw, Quw’utsun and Tla’amin, on whose traditional lands we teach, learn,\n                                                                                        research, live and share knowledge. Accreditation Terms Emergency Information Website Feedback © 2021 Vancouver Island University MENU CLOSE X Future Students International Students Current Students Employees Alumni & Donors Contact VIU Main Menu Open submenu (About VIU) About VIU Open submenu (Programs and Courses) Programs and Courses Open submenu (Admissions) Admissions Facebook Instagram Twitter Youtube LinkedIn VIU RSS feed Close submenu (About VIU) About VIU Why VIU Campus Information Athletics Close submenu (Programs and Courses) Programs and Courses Open submenu (Areas of Study) Areas of Study Courses Apply Now Close submenu (Areas of Study) Areas of Study Open submenu (Academic and Career Preparation) Academic and Career Preparation Open submenu (Art, Design and Performing Arts) Art, Design and Performing Arts Open submenu (Arts, Humanities and Social Sciences) Arts, Humanities and Social Sciences Open submenu (Business Management) Business Management Open submenu (Education) Education English as a Second Language (ESL) Exploratory University Studies Open submenu (First Nations) First Nations Graduate Programs Open submenu (Health) Health Open submenu (Human Services) Human Services Natural Resource Extension Program Online Programs / Distance Courses Open submenu (Professional Development and Training) Professional Development and Training Open submen