      "title": "Professor, Sociology",
      "description": "Professor, Sociology (3059) | VIU | Vancouver Island University //>\r\n    <!--\r\n    (function(i,s,o,g,r,a,m){i[\"GoogleAnalyticsObject\"]=r;i[r]=i[r]||function(){(i[r].q=i[r].q||[]).push(arguments)},i[r].l=1*new Date();a=s.createElement(o),m=s.getElementsByTagName(o)[0];a.async=1;a.src=g;m.parentNode.insertBefore(a,m)})(window,document,\"script\",\"//www.google-analytics.com/analytics.js\",\"ga\");ga(\"create\", \"UA-168470-11\", {\"cookieDomain\":\"auto\",\"allowLinker\":true});ga(\"require\", \"linker\");ga(\"linker:autoLink\", [\"www.viu.ca\",\"programs.viu.ca\"]);ga(\"send\", \"pageview\");setTimeout(function(){var a=document.createElement(\"script\");\r\n    var b=document.getElementsByTagName(\"script\")[0];\r\n    a.src=document.location.protocol+\"//script.crazyegg.com/pages/scripts/0056/6315.js?\"+Math.floor(new Date().getTime()/3600000);\r\n    a.async=true;a.type=\"text/javascript\";b.parentNode.insertBefore(a,b)}, 1);\r\n    //-->\r\n    <! Skip to main content VIU Future Students International Students Current Students Employees Alumni & Donors Contact Registration Registration Space tasks Map Members Space Structure Registration Site map Parents viu.ca Sections Pages All Sites... All Groups... Site Members Registration Member list Admins admin boquist culvers manhasm2 testuser Members No members Professor, Sociology (3059) Professor, Sociology Employment Group VIUFA Position Number 00207 Division Faculty of Social Sciences Department Sociology Campus Nanaimo and/or Cowichan  *Successful candidates must be able to attend in person on campus as required. Location Multiple Locations, British Columbia Country Canada Appointment Type regular full-time FTE 1 Workload Teach eight 3-credit courses per year for full-time 1.0 FTE Pay Level VIUFA F2: $71,141 - $114,001 per annum (prorated if part-time). Starting Salary Faculty are placed on the salary scale based on education, experience and placement criteria as outlined in the Collective Agreement Start: Duties begin August 16, 2027 Appointment Start Date 01-Aug-2027 Additional Information Review of Applications Commences: Late Fall 2026 Potential Interview Dates: Early 2027 Applicant Documents CV/Resume,\nCover Letter,\nQualifications ,\nName and contact information of recent supervisors willing to provide a reference,\nResearch Posted Date 24-Sep-2026 Closing Date 06-Jan-2027 Job Reference 3059 Duties: We invite applications from university educators seeking to join a collegial department where teaching innovation and student success are highly valued. We seek applicants who share our passion for delivering high-quality undergraduate education and who can skillfully bridge their teaching with their scholarly work. We are exploring our curriculum and program learning outcomes, and we invite applicants who are excited about contributing to shaping the future of our department. We welcome sociologists interested in interdisciplinary collaboration within the social sciences, particularly with the department of Anthropology. We seek to hire an individual whose scholarly experience speaks to contemporary issues with expertise in areas that complement those already in the Department. Priority will be given to individuals with an interest in developing new courses for the program and creating engaging learning opportunities for undergraduate students. The teaching responsibilities of successful candidates may include research methods. Course descriptions and more information about the Sociology Department are available on their program page . Candidates must demonstrate commitment to teaching, learning and student success through scholarship and institutional service. Successful candidates will participate in a wide range of activities outside the classroom, including student support; institutional, faculty and departmental committee meetings and other initiatives; and professional activities in keeping with their disciplines in and outside the institution. Required Qualifications: An earned PhD in Sociology from an accredited institution. Recent experience and demonstrated excellence in teaching undergraduate Sociology courses. Research experience that supports the development of new courses and the mentoring of undergraduate researchers. Participation in professional development activities. Demonstrated proficiency with technology relevant to the position. Preferred Qualifications: Experience teaching small classes in an inclusive institutional environment. A record of institutional service. Please submit: CV/Resume Cover letter highlighting relevant experience and education. Copies of transcripts/credentials/qualifications identified on resume A statement outlining research interests. Teaching dossier including a statement of teaching philosophy, teaching evaluations and a sample of course outlines. Name and contact information for three people willing to provide a reference VIU is pleased to offer eligible employees a comprehensive benefit plan; ample paid holiday time; professional development opportunities and a desirable pension plan. As part of the VIU campus community, our employees work with supportive colleagues within an encouraging environment and are provided with the tools and training that promote learning and development. The perks of VIU employment are multiple, and include well-being initiatives and services, strategic discounts, and flexible work opportunities. Note: Short-listed candidates must provide original transcripts, or applicable original certifications at time of interview. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Vancouver Island University (VIU) is collectively committed to building and sustaining a diverse and inclusive working and learning environment for faculty, staff, and students.  In our journey towards greater diversity, we invite applications from members of equity-seeking communities including women, racialized and Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, persons of all gender identities and sexual orientations who bring value to the VIU community through their lived experiences.  We encourage members of all equity-seeking groups to self-identify within their application cover letter.  When a candidate voluntarily discloses this information in their cover letter, the information will be used only for the fulfillment of the career opportunity.  Disclosure and/or self-identification with an equity-seeking group will not lead to advantageous treatment of a candidate who is not qualified. #INDHP Apply for this job Send to a friend About VIU Careers at VIU Employee Directory Parking Academics International Students Library Programs and Courses VIU Learn Campuses Nanaimo (Main Campus) Cowichan Parksville-Qualicum Centre tiwɛmawtxʷ (Powell River) About VIU Why VIU? Careers at VIU Employee Directory VIU Facts Events News Parking University Governance Academics Admission Requirements Dual Credit Financial Aid and Awards Graduate Programs International Students Library Online Education Programs and Courses Registration Transfer Students VIU Learn Student Life Student Housing Campus Recreation Campus Store Food Services Health and Wellness Services for Students VIU Mariners Athletics Campuses Campus Information Nanaimo (Main Campus) Cowichan Parksville-Qualicum Centre tiwɛmawtxʷ (Powell River) Vancouver Island University Nanaimo (Main Campus) 900 Fifth Street Nanaimo, BC V9R 5S5 Canada 250.753.3245 1.888.920.2221 info@viu.ca Facebook Instagram Twitter Youtube LinkedIn VIU RSS feed The VIU community acknowledges and thanks the Snuneymuxw, Quwutsun and Tlaamin, on whose traditional lands we teach, learn,\r\n                                                                                        research, live and share knowledge. Accreditation Terms Emergency Information Website Feedback © 2021 Vancouver Island University MENU CLOSE X Future Students Internationa