    "https://careers.viu.ca/vacancy/instructor-theatre-history-604008.html": {
      "title": "Instructor, Theatre History",
      "description": "Instructor, Theatre History (3055) | VIU | Vancouver Island University //>\r\n    <!--\r\n    (function(i,s,o,g,r,a,m){i[\"GoogleAnalyticsObject\"]=r;i[r]=i[r]||function(){(i[r].q=i[r].q||[]).push(arguments)},i[r].l=1*new Date();a=s.createElement(o),m=s.getElementsByTagName(o)[0];a.async=1;a.src=g;m.parentNode.insertBefore(a,m)})(window,document,\"script\",\"//www.google-analytics.com/analytics.js\",\"ga\");ga(\"create\", \"UA-168470-11\", {\"cookieDomain\":\"auto\",\"allowLinker\":true});ga(\"require\", \"linker\");ga(\"linker:autoLink\", [\"www.viu.ca\",\"programs.viu.ca\"]);ga(\"send\", \"pageview\");setTimeout(function(){var a=document.createElement(\"script\");\r\n    var b=document.getElementsByTagName(\"script\")[0];\r\n    a.src=document.location.protocol+\"//script.crazyegg.com/pages/scripts/0056/6315.js?\"+Math.floor(new Date().getTime()/3600000);\r\n    a.async=true;a.type=\"text/javascript\";b.parentNode.insertBefore(a,b)}, 1);\r\n    //-->\r\n    <! Skip to main content VIU Future Students International Students Current Students Employees Alumni & Donors Contact Registration Registration Space tasks Map Members Space Structure Registration Site map Parents viu.ca Sections Pages All Sites... All Groups... Site Members Registration Member list Admins admin boquist culvers manhasm2 testuser Members No members Instructor, Theatre History (3055) Instructor, Theatre History For the past 50 years the Theatre Department has been training professionals in the entertainment industry. Inside of our two-year program, we work closely with the students in an ensemble setting. Bringing in industry professionals, as well as working closely with the arts community, we supply our students with an array of experience that prepares them for work in the field. Small class sizes, community opportunities, and individual support makes the Theatre Department at VIU an ideal place of employment for anyone in the performing arts. Employment Group VIUFA Position Number 00382 Division Faculty of Arts and Humanities Department Theatre Campus Nanaimo campus  *Successful candidates must be able to attend in person on campus as required. Location Nanaimo, British Columbia Country Canada Appointment Type temporary part-time Workload Two courses (six hours of instruction) in each the Spring and Fall semesters plus office hours Pay Level VIUFA F2: temporary instructional. Starting Salary $8,196.30 per assigned course consisting of three workload hours. The rate for any courses requiring fewer or greater hours shall be prorated based on this standard. Appointment Start Date 04-Jan-2027 Appointment End Date 31-Dec-2027 Leave Replacement Appointment may be extended or end early, depending on return of incumbent. Additional Information Spring 2027 semester contract dates: January 4 to May 21, 2027; Fall 2027 semester contract dates: August 16 to December 31, 2027, with a break in employment between the semesters. Subject to funding and enrollment. Applicant Documents CV/Resume,\nCover Letter,\nName and contact information of recent supervisors willing to provide a reference Posted Date 24-Sep-2026 Closing Date 21-Oct-2026 Job Reference 3055 Documents VIUFA Sessional Workload Examples (PDF , 92.46kb) Duties: The successful candidate will develop, prepare and deliver lectures, and seminars to students in the Theatre Department commencing with the Spring 2027 semester and then the Fall 2027 semester subject to a successful evaluation in the Spring. Faculty are responsible for preparing and delivering classes, designing and grading student assignments and tests, facilitating the students' integration of theory and practice, holding weekly office hours, and evaluating student progress. Secondary responsibilities include record keeping and general department curriculum maintenance as pertains to the courses being taught. The following two courses are timetabled in the Spring 2027 semester: THEA 112: Theatre History I Tuesday and Thursday 10:00-11:30 THEA 212: Theatre History III Tuesday and Thursday 13:00-14:30 The Fall 2027 courses will be (possibly subject to change): THEA 111: Introduction to Theatre Tuesday and Thursday 10:00-11:30 THEA 211: Theatre History II Tuesday and Thursday 13:00-14:30 Candidates must demonstrate commitment to teaching, learning and student success through scholarship and institutional service. Successful candidates will participate in a wide range of activities outside the classroom, including student support; institutional, faculty and departmental committee meetings and other initiatives; and professional activities in keeping with their disciplines in and outside the institution. Required Qualifications: Master's degree in related field from an appropriately accredited institution and a minimum four years' recent experience. A combination of education and experience may be considered for candidates with exceptional demonstrated experience. Education and experience with related fields to course description Recent teaching or lecturing experience with adults at the post-secondary level Strong general background in theatre and/or performing arts Demonstrated interpersonal skills working as a team member Strong organizational skills and demonstrated ability to meet deadlines Excellent written and oral communication skills Sensitivity to the needs of a wide variety of adult students Preferred Qualifications: PHD or Master's degree in Theatre History or a related discipline Industry Affiliations in appropriate area Experience developing course material and curriculum Experience with publishing course material to a Learning Management System VIU is pleased to offer eligible employees a comprehensive benefit plan; ample paid holiday time; professional development opportunities and a desirable pension plan. As part of the VIU campus community, our employees work with supportive colleagues within an encouraging environment and are provided with the tools and training that promote learning and development. The perks of VIU employment are multiple, and include well-being initiatives and services, strategic discounts, and flexible work opportunities. Note: Short-listed candidates must provide original transcripts, or applicable original certifications at time of interview. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Vancouver Island University (VIU) is collectively committed to building and sustaining a diverse and inclusive working and learning environment for faculty, staff, and students.  In our journey towards greater diversity, we invite applications from members of equity-seeking communities including women, racialized and Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, persons of all gender identities and sexual orientations who bring value to the VIU community through their lived experiences.  We encourage members of all equity-seeking groups to self-identify within their application cover letter.  When a candidate voluntarily discloses this information in their cover letter, the information will be used only for the fulfillment of the career opportunity.  Disclosure and/or self-identification with an equity-seeking group will not lead to advantageous treatment of a candidate who is not qualified. Apply for this job Send to a friend About VIU Careers at VIU Employee Directory Parking Academics International Students Library Programs and Courses VIU Learn Campuses Nanaimo (Main Campus) Cowichan Parksville-Qualicum Centre tiwɛmawtxʷ (Powell River) About VIU Why VIU? Careers at VIU Employee Directory VIU Facts Events News Parking University Governance Academics Admission Requirements Dual Credit Financial Aid and Awards Graduate Programs International Students Library Online Education Programs and Courses Registration Transfer Students VIU Learn Student Life Student Housing Campus Recreation Campus Store Food Services Health and Wellness Services for Students VIU 