ction Studies Certificate Advanced Diploma in GIS Applicatons Diploma in Criminology Master of Geographic Information Systems Applications Master of Community Planning Post Degree-Diploma in Languages and Culture (Romance Languages) Proficiency in Language and Culture Certificate Business Management Applied Business Technology Bachelor of Business Administration Business Fundamental for Aboriginal Communities Certificate Certificate in Business Management Diploma in Business Administration Executive Professional Development Forensic Accounting and Fraud Investigation Advanced Diploma (Online) Graduate Certificate in Business Management Skills for Supervisors Master of Business Administration Post-Degree Diploma in Business Studies Education Bachelor of Education Bachelor of EducationPost Baccalaureate Degree (full-time) Global Education Graduate Diploma Inclusive Education (Special Education) Graduate Diploma Master of Education in Educational Leadership Master of Education in Special Education Online Learning and Teaching Graduate Diploma Bachelor of Arts, Physical Education Physical Education Diploma Special Education Teacher Specialty Post Degree Diploma Program (SETS) Teacher Leadership Graduate Diploma English as a Second Language (ESL) Exploratory University Studies First Nations Arts One-First Nations Child and Youth Care First Nations Graduate Programs Health Activity Assistant Bachelor of Science in Nursing Community Health Promotion for Aboriginal Communities Community Mental Health Worker Dental Assistant Dental Hygiene Graduate Diploma in Gerontology: Active Aging Health Care Assistant Practical Nursing Human Services Bachelor of Arts in Child and Youth Care Bachelor of Social Work Child and Youth Care Leadership and Disability Studies Early Childhood Education and Care School and Community Support Worker Social Services Education Assistand and Community Support Natural Resource Extension Program Online Programs / Distance Courses Professional Development and Training British Columbia First Nations Building Inspector Building Service Worker Hospital Unit Coordinator Managing Conflict In The Workplace Master Gardener Program Medical Device Reprocessing Technician Medical Office Assistant Professional Esthetics Science and Technology Bachelor of Science, Majors, Minors and Transfer Biology Chemistry Computer Science Earth Science Geography Geoscience Mathematics Physics Psychology Bachelor of Science in Fisheries and Aquaculture Bachelor of Natural Resource Protection Diploma in Computing Science Fisheries and Aquaculture Technology Forest Resources Technology Fundamental of Engineering Certificate Program Post-Degree Diploma in Fisheries and Aquaculture Resource Management Officer Technology The High School at VIU Tourism, Recreation and Hospitality Bachelor of Hospitality Management Bachelor of Tourism Management Culinary Arts Bridging to Bachelor of Hospitality Management Event Management Certificate Hospitality Management Diploma Master of Arts in Sustainable Leisure Management Recreation and Sport Management Graduate Diploma in Sustainable Leisure Management Tourism Studies Wine Business Certificate in Adventure Tourism and Recreation Trades and Applied Technology Aboriginal Construction Aluminum Boat Building Applied Business Technology - Online Automotive Service Technician Carpentry Culinary Arts Culinary Management Electrician First Nations Housing Manager Hairdressing Heavy Equipment Operator Heavy Mechanical Trades Foundation Horticultral Technician Foundation Information Technology and Applied Systems Motorcycle and Marine Technician Power Engineering/Process Operator - 4th Class Professional Baking and Pastry Arts Refrigeration Air-Conditioning Mechanic Welding Teaching English as a Second or Foreign Language Courses Apply Now Admissions Admission Requirements Requirements Equivalencies and Advanced Placement Program How to Order Transcripts Tuition & Fees Fees Tuition Payment of Fees Financial Aid & Aw