    "https://careers.viu.ca/vacancy/administrative-assistant-extended-604053.html": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant (Extended)",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant (Extended)  (3064) | VIU | Vancouver Island University //>\r\n    <!--\r\n    (function(i,s,o,g,r,a,m){i[\"GoogleAnalyticsObject\"]=r;i[r]=i[r]||function(){(i[r].q=i[r].q||[]).push(arguments)},i[r].l=1*new Date();a=s.createElement(o),m=s.getElementsByTagName(o)[0];a.async=1;a.src=g;m.parentNode.insertBefore(a,m)})(window,document,\"script\",\"//www.google-analytics.com/analytics.js\",\"ga\");ga(\"create\", \"UA-168470-11\", {\"cookieDomain\":\"auto\",\"allowLinker\":true});ga(\"require\", \"linker\");ga(\"linker:autoLink\", [\"www.viu.ca\",\"programs.viu.ca\"]);ga(\"send\", \"pageview\");setTimeout(function(){var a=document.createElement(\"script\");\r\n    var b=document.getElementsByTagName(\"script\")[0];\r\n    a.src=document.location.protocol+\"//script.crazyegg.com/pages/scripts/0056/6315.js?\"+Math.floor(new Date().getTime()/3600000);\r\n    a.async=true;a.type=\"text/javascript\";b.parentNode.insertBefore(a,b)}, 1);\r\n    //-->\r\n    <! Skip to main content VIU Future Students International Students Current Students Employees Alumni & Donors Contact Registration Registration Space tasks Map Members Space Structure Registration Site map Parents viu.ca Sections Pages All Sites... All Groups... Site Members Registration Member list Admins admin boquist culvers manhasm2 testuser Members No members Administrative Assistant (Extended)  (3064) Administrative Assistant (Extended) Employment Group CUPE Position Number 00116 Division Faculty of Academic and Career Preparation Department English Language Learning Department Campus Nanaimo campus  *Successful candidates must be able to attend in person on campus as required. Location Nanaimo, British Columbia Country Canada Appointment Type regular full-time FTE 1.00 Workload 35 hours per week, Monday to Friday Pay Level CUPE 8: $31.48 per hour Appointment Start Date 30-Nov-2026 Additional Information Appointment start date may adjust to accommodate the hire process timing. Applicant Documents CV/Resume,\nCover Letter,\nQualifications ,\nName and contact information of recent supervisors willing to provide a reference Posted Date 08-Oct-2026 Closing Date 28-Oct-2026 Job Reference 3064 Documents CUPE Self-Declaration Form (Word , 40.35kb) Duties: Provide front-line customer service for students, faculty and the general public in person, by phone and by email. Work closely with Registration, Records, and Financial Aid, and provide information and respond to inquiries from the Welcome Centre, Advising, Accessibility Services and The Gathering Place. Maintain privacy and confidentiality. Provide administrative support to Academic and Career Preparation programs including: Adult Basic Education, Literacy, Workplace Essential Skills and Training, Indigenous University Bridging, English Language Learners, and Volunteer Tutor Program. Provide assistance, training, and guidance to faculty and staff on assessment processes and departmental procedures. Review transcripts, course enrolment requirements/prerequisites, or assessment results and initiate a course of action for students (e.g., register, refer to an advisor or department Chairs). Monitor class waitlists. Meet cyclical demands of course offerings, design and prepare brochures, information sheets, schedules, calendars, timetables and packages; design and create spreadsheets, charts, reports, forms, pamphlets, or other written material. Order and manage textbooks and textbook loans. Order supplies, schedule meetings, take minutes, distribute mail, maintain and troubleshoot office equipment. Complete general updates on the administrative area, faculty or department website (e.g., biographies, announcements, important dates, course information), ensuring information is current and accurate. Required Qualifications: One-year certificate in Office Administration, or equivalent, from an appropriately accredited institution. Minimum of three years of experience in higher education administration. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be considered. Demonstrated relational database understanding; ability to use spreadsheet software features; demonstrated intercultural experience; patience and excellent communication skills; ability to work in a busy, changing environment that requires the ability to shift detailed focus quickly. Students are English language learners and often new to Canada; therefore, this position requires a high level of intercultural competency. Experience with Access databases and SAWS. Excellent knowledge of Excel. Preferred Qualifications: Two-year diploma in a related field from an appropriately accredited institution. Experience in educational programming context, e.g., familiarity with faculty support, student support, and timetabling. Training in intercultural communication and / or intercultural conflict resolution. Proficiency in a language other than English. Valid class 5 BC Driver's License and have a confirmed satisfactory driving record. VIU is pleased to offer eligible employees a comprehensive benefit plan; ample paid holiday time; professional development opportunities and a desirable pension plan. As part of the VIU campus community, our employees work with supportive colleagues within an encouraging environment and are provided with the tools and training that promote learning and development. The perks of VIU employment are multiple, and include well-being initiatives and services, strategic discounts, and flexible work opportunities. Note: Short-listed candidates must provide original transcripts, or applicable original certifications at time of interview. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. Vancouver Island University (VIU) is collectively committed to building and sustaining a diverse and inclusive working and learning environment for faculty, staff, and students.  In our journey towards greater diversity, we invite applications from members of equity-seeking communities including women, racialized and Indigenous persons, persons with disabilities, persons of all gender identities and sexual orientations who bring value to the VIU community through their lived experiences.  We encourage members of all equity-seeking groups to self-identify within their application cover letter.  When a candidate voluntarily discloses this information in their cover letter, the information will be used only for the fulfillment of the career opportunity.  Disclosure and/or self-identification with an equity-seeking group will not lead to advantageous treatment of a candidate who is not qualified. Apply for this job Send to a friend About VIU Careers at VIU Employee Directory Parking Academics International Students Library Programs and Courses VIU Learn Campuses Nanaimo (Main Campus) Cowichan Parksville-Qualicum Centre tiwɛmawtxʷ (Powell River) About VIU Why VIU? Careers at VIU Employee Directory VIU Facts Events News Parking University Governance Academics Admission Requirements Dual Credit Financial Aid and Awards Graduate Programs International Students Library Online Education Programs and Courses Registration Transfer Students VIU Learn Student Life Student Housing Campus Recreation Campus Store Food Services Health and Wellness Services for Students VIU Mariners Athletics Campuses Campus Information Nanaimo (Main Campus) Cowichan Parksville-Qualicum Centre tiwɛmawtxʷ (Powell River) Vancouver Island University Nanaimo (Main Campus) 900 Fifth Street Nanaimo, BC V9R 5S5 Canada 250.753.3245 1.888.920.2221 info@viu.ca Facebook Instagram Twitter Youtube LinkedIn VIU RSS feed The VIU community acknowledges and thanks the Snuneymuxw, Quwutsun and Tlaamin, on whose traditional lands we teach, learn,\r\n                                                                                        research, live and share knowledge. Accreditation Terms Emergency Information Website Feedback © 2021 